1
00:00:00,520 --> 00:00:01,280
=You Alone Know Me=

2
00:00:01,280 --> 00:00:03,892
(From the Qimao novel "My Bestie's Icy
Dad Got Drunk and Wild After We Wed")

3
00:00:03,892 --> 00:00:04,920
(Written by Qiaoqiaojiang)

4
00:00:05,120 --> 00:00:08,040
=Episode 10=

5
00:00:32,759 --> 00:00:34,000
Next, Lin Hua.

6
00:00:36,719 --> 00:00:37,759
(So she's Lin Hua.)

7
00:00:38,719 --> 00:00:39,920
(I'd better get this right)

8
00:00:40,240 --> 00:00:41,119
(for Miss Li.)

9
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:46,320
Wait.

10
00:00:51,600 --> 00:00:53,440
(Resume of Lin Hua, Master
of Architecture, Jiangcheng University)

11
00:00:53,479 --> 00:00:55,039
You're Lin Hua, an architecture major
from Jiangcheng University?

12
00:00:56,399 --> 00:00:57,079
You don't need to go in.

13
00:01:00,280 --> 00:01:00,840
Why not?

14
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:02,679
You lied on your resume. No interview.

15
00:01:03,320 --> 00:01:05,760
S&D doesn't hire dishonest students.

16
00:01:07,960 --> 00:01:09,400
(Zhao Song, HR Manager)

17
00:01:11,159 --> 00:01:11,719
Mr. Zhao,

18
00:01:12,280 --> 00:01:13,959
if you think my credentials are false,

19
00:01:14,319 --> 00:01:14,840
I've included

20
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:16,560
proof of all my design work.

21
00:01:16,840 --> 00:01:17,840
S&D interviews

22
00:01:17,920 --> 00:01:19,079
follow a strict review process.

23
00:01:19,319 --> 00:01:21,079
No one can cancel one on a whim.

24
00:01:21,599 --> 00:01:23,640
I'm sure you know company policy.

25
00:01:23,959 --> 00:01:24,680
So I'm asking for

26
00:01:24,959 --> 00:01:26,400
an interview through that process.

27
00:01:26,640 --> 00:01:27,599
You're disqualified.

28
00:01:27,799 --> 00:01:28,680
Appeal if you want.

29
00:01:29,040 --> 00:01:30,319
But even if you do,

30
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:31,920
we still won't hire you.

31
00:01:32,400 --> 00:01:33,560
(I had no idea)

32
00:01:33,760 --> 00:01:35,519
(our human resources manager)

33
00:01:35,680 --> 00:01:37,439
(had the final say over all of S&D.)

34
00:01:48,200 --> 00:01:49,000
Ms. Xie.

35
00:01:50,319 --> 00:01:51,079
What brings you here?

36
00:01:52,040 --> 00:01:53,079
Architecture at Jiangcheng University?

37
00:01:54,400 --> 00:01:55,439
Yes, Ms. Xie.

38
00:01:55,760 --> 00:01:57,400
Come in. I'll interview you myself.

39
00:02:05,760 --> 00:02:06,200
(What?)

40
00:02:17,120 --> 00:02:18,000
I've ordered for you.

41
00:02:22,280 --> 00:02:23,120
What's wrong?

42
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:25,639
You passed the interview, didn't you?

43
00:02:26,520 --> 00:02:27,479
Why the long face?

44
00:02:27,759 --> 00:02:28,360
Not happy?

45
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:29,599
It's nothing.

46
00:02:30,080 --> 00:02:31,719
During the interview,

47
00:02:31,879 --> 00:02:33,560
there was a little hiccup.

48
00:02:34,520 --> 00:02:35,400
But it's all sorted out.

49
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:36,800
Good.

50
00:02:40,159 --> 00:02:40,879
By the way, Hua,

51
00:02:41,439 --> 00:02:43,680
I've been meaning to tell you something.

52
00:02:46,919 --> 00:02:48,759
My dad isn't my biological father.

53
00:02:51,800 --> 00:02:53,360
My birth parents

54
00:02:53,479 --> 00:02:55,719
were researchers working in Africa.

55
00:02:56,319 --> 00:02:57,560
War broke out,

56
00:02:58,599 --> 00:03:00,199
and my birth dad died on duty.

57
00:03:01,280 --> 00:03:02,199
My birth mom

58
00:03:02,599 --> 00:03:04,280
had a difficult delivery.

59
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:06,919
She didn't make it, either.

60
00:03:07,719 --> 00:03:09,520
To give me legal status

61
00:03:11,319 --> 00:03:13,479
so I wouldn't be sent back
as a war orphan

62
00:03:13,960 --> 00:03:15,120
or put in an orphanage,

63
00:03:15,800 --> 00:03:16,879
my dad, Xie Zhouhan,

64
00:03:17,159 --> 00:03:19,120
signed a marriage agreement with her

65
00:03:19,479 --> 00:03:19,960
and married her.

66
00:03:22,319 --> 00:03:23,280
So

67
00:03:24,199 --> 00:03:25,439
back then, he...

68
00:03:26,159 --> 00:03:28,439
His family said he'd disgraced them.

69
00:03:28,800 --> 00:03:30,599
Grandma Xie nearly passed out.

70
00:03:31,240 --> 00:03:31,719
Later,

71
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:33,479
he brought me back from Africa.

72
00:03:33,879 --> 00:03:34,919
He lived with that rumor

73
00:03:35,240 --> 00:03:37,039
for over ten years

74
00:03:37,759 --> 00:03:39,159
without ever explaining.

75
00:03:40,159 --> 00:03:41,680
So that's why he...

76
00:03:45,199 --> 00:03:46,120
So, Hua,

77
00:03:47,639 --> 00:03:48,719
please be

78
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:50,800
a little nicer to my dad.

79
00:03:53,159 --> 00:03:53,560
Of course,

80
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:57,039
if he ever lets you down,

81
00:03:57,439 --> 00:03:58,639
we'll take everything he has

82
00:03:59,520 --> 00:04:00,319
and leave him all alone.

83
00:04:00,759 --> 00:04:01,520
He won't.

84
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:06,960
He's a good man.

85
00:04:07,879 --> 00:04:08,800
He won't grow old alone.

86
00:04:10,759 --> 00:04:13,039
That's my bestie.

87
00:04:13,280 --> 00:04:14,039
I picked the right girl.

88
00:04:16,120 --> 00:04:16,839
Hey, Zhouhan,

89
00:04:17,560 --> 00:04:18,519
I see now

90
00:04:19,160 --> 00:04:20,319
why you recommended her.

91
00:04:22,319 --> 00:04:23,959
Thanks for finding me such a gem.

92
00:04:24,759 --> 00:04:25,800
I've always been a good judge of people.

93
00:04:26,279 --> 00:04:26,959
She said

94
00:04:27,920 --> 00:04:29,000
buildings have warmth.

95
00:04:30,439 --> 00:04:31,920
She reminds me of you at her age.

96
00:04:33,360 --> 00:04:34,120
She's good.

97
00:04:34,959 --> 00:04:35,879
I'll buy you dinner sometime.

98
00:04:44,759 --> 00:04:45,480
You passed the interview?

99
00:04:47,360 --> 00:04:49,000
Ms. Xie put me on the director's team.

100
00:04:49,279 --> 00:04:50,120
And I'll be learning

101
00:04:50,279 --> 00:04:52,279
from S&D's chief designer, Wayne.

102
00:04:53,079 --> 00:04:53,720
Wayne

103
00:04:54,480 --> 00:04:55,759
is a genius in the industry.

104
00:04:56,600 --> 00:04:58,360
He's tough, but he values talent.

105
00:04:59,160 --> 00:05:01,040
You'll learn a lot from him.

106
00:05:05,720 --> 00:05:06,600
What would you like for dinner?

107
00:05:06,839 --> 00:05:07,600
Let's celebrate.

108
00:05:27,960 --> 00:05:28,900
♪You say you♪

109
00:05:28,900 --> 00:05:30,920
♪Don't need anyone♪
(Signature page, Party A Xie Zhouhan)

110
00:05:31,280 --> 00:05:34,320
♪You're just fine on your own♪

111
00:05:34,640 --> 00:05:37,480
♪I see the pride behind your smile♪

112
00:05:37,600 --> 00:05:40,480
♪And the pain you face at night♪

113
00:05:41,240 --> 00:05:44,160
♪Sometimes love isn't about possession♪

114
00:05:44,560 --> 00:05:47,320
♪It's tenderness that sets you free♪

115
00:05:47,400 --> 00:05:50,400
♪Some love needs no promises♪

116
00:05:50,520 --> 00:05:53,760
♪I'll face this cold world with you♪

117
00:05:53,840 --> 00:05:56,440
♪I keep my feelings safely hidden♪

118
00:05:56,560 --> 00:05:59,680
♪Quietly staying behind you♪

119
00:05:59,880 --> 00:06:02,640
♪I'm right behind you♪

120
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:06,160
♪Shielding you from every hidden storm♪

121
00:06:06,240 --> 00:06:08,800
♪Keeping the rain out of your eyes♪

122
00:06:08,800 --> 00:06:12,800
♪So you can walk ahead without fear♪

123
00:06:15,800 --> 00:06:19,000
♪I'm right behind you♪

124
00:06:19,160 --> 00:06:20,880
♪Waiting for you to turn around♪

125
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:22,720
♪Waiting for you to finally see♪

126
00:06:22,800 --> 00:06:25,160
♪You're the only one I lose control for♪

127
00:06:25,360 --> 00:06:26,720
♪I'm right behind you♪

128
00:06:26,800 --> 00:06:29,080
♪Loving you gently, though no one knows♪

129
00:06:29,200 --> 00:06:30,840
♪I won't claim you♪

130
00:06:30,960 --> 00:06:32,520
♪I won't ask you to stay♪

131
00:06:32,640 --> 00:06:35,200
♪I'll spend the rest of my life♪

132
00:06:36,240 --> 00:06:38,560
♪Waiting for you♪
